[Music]  hi everyone i am alam javed  i am an undergrad final year student  at amit university noida india  i am a research fellow at mind biotech  and the  project i'm currently working on is  identification of biomarkers leading to  alzheimer's based on rna sequence of  artistic and control cortex  so alzheimer's disease is  a disease which affects mostly the brain  and causes a symptom called dementia  it is said to be progressive cerebrum  disorder which is irreversible and that  gradually destroys thinking ability and  old memories  it is said to be a disorder which is  irreversible and that gradually destroys  thinking ability and old memories  in this picture you can see how a  healthy brain  gets affected by alzheimer's disease  alzheimer's disease and autistic  spectrum disorder  autism spectrum disorder and alzheimer's  disease are neurodevelopmental and  neurodegenerative disorders respectively  with devastating effects  it is of utmost curiosity that these  disorders  express at different stages of life and  there is an involvement of certain  susceptible genes  this genetic basis makes the background  of common associations like memory  deficiency cognition changes  demyelination oxidative stress and  inflammation  an integral part of food disorders  the methodology  which i used was a pipeline was run  using the data set  which was rna sequence of autistic  control cortex a comparison was made  between the autistic and control cortex  genes  comparative analysis done to analyze the  sample between the groups by  running the expression pipeline on t  bioinfo server  as a result desect 2 was used to obtain  differential express genes enrichment  analysis is used to obtain gang pathways  gse  functional enrichment analysis was used  to obtain geo-enriched pathways  and the network  comparative analysis comparative  analysis consists of pipelines to obtain  differentially expressed genes keck  pathways geo-enriched genes among the  groups  desect 2 is a tool used for differential  gene expression analysis of rna sequence  data  enrichment analysis identifies  biological pathways that is keg pathways  gsea analysis is done to determine set  of genes which show statistically  significant concordant differences  between two biological states that is go  pathway  like here we can see how the pipeline  was run  first we click on the start button v  and then desect 2  is selected then enrichment analysis and  gsa  according to the requirement and then we  end the pipeline the parameters are  fed into the pipeline  volcano plot buff it is performed under  the two conditions the adjusted p  p-value at y-axis  and  log to full change at x-axis  uh it determines significant  differentially expressed genes genes  which are having negative log to full  change value will be considered  will be considered as downregulated  genes whereas the positive log to full  change value to be considered as  upregulated genes  it basically determines significant  differentially expressed genes  the blue  the blue area represents  significant genes and red area  represents significant  differentially expressed genes  genes which are having  negative log-to-fold change value will  be considered as downregulated value  whereas  positive log to full change value as  upregulated value basically the higher  gene in the plot is more significance  keg enriched pathways  keck provides information of enrichment  of genes in the area displayed on the  basis of two parameters count and p  adjusted  value which shows distribution of genes  as you can see here that count shows the  number of genes involved in the pathway  and color represents the  adjusted value  keng enrich pathways provides  information about various pathways that  are either are activated or suppressed  due to the upregulation or down  regulation of the gene respectively  pathways corresponding to the highest  quantity of upregulated genes are highly  activated and pathways corresponding to  higher count  sorry number down regulated genes are  highly suppressed so basically the  highest count of upregulated genes is  associated with  cytokine cytokine interactions as you  can see here  it has the highest count number  and the down related gene is associated  with tca or citrate cycle as we can see  it over here  network blocked it is basically a graph  that analyzes the pathways in the  network based on the full change value  size of dot in the code depicts the  number of genes involved in particular  pathway the color indicates the full  change value  it analyzes the genes that are included  in the particular pathway the dot size  depicts the number of genes involved  color of the  dot  full change value shows the full change  value and decrease in the fold change  leads to increase in gene expressed in  pathway as we can see that there are a  few core hub genes which over here  are  is  n  l r  and over here it is sox4 cnmd  and tspo  so the key findings which  i have noted from keg analysis is  possible association can be made between  suppressed pathway of citrix cycle or  tsa and cytokine cytogram receptor  interaction  from volcano plot the an upregulated  genes  is lil rb1 and  socs3  also we found hub genes which can be  used as biomarker network plot which are  n  l rp9 elf 4 tspo cnmd  future directions researchers can  perform experiments focusing on these  particular  gene found in the study and correlate  their upregulated down and down  regulated genes with disease progression  thank you so much  [Music]  you

